-- title:
--   Special-fibre geometry of Pic⁰ for the X₁(Mp) model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ with primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and let $K\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in its image, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of $\mathtt{jq}$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and an $A$-algebra. Over $k$ are given two proper smooth geometrically integral relative curves $c_1,c_2$ and closed immersions $i_1,i_2$ of them, over $k$, into the base change to $k$ of the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) (the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebras generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$); the images of $i_1,i_2$ cover that special fibre, the scheme-theoretic intersection $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$ is reduced with $n>0$ points. Further data: a section $\varepsilon$ of the model over $A$, sections $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2$ of $c_1,c_2$ with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equal to the base-changed $\varepsilon$; a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation $D$ over $A$ for the model (a scheme $D.P$ with structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section) which represents, for the cut `algEquivZeroCut` of fibrewise algebraically trivial rigidified line bundles, the rigidified relative Picard functor, with $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ smooth and separated; an explicit representing datum `hreps` (Poincaré bundle plus universal property) for the base change $D_k$ with the base-changed section; designations $D_1,D_2$ over $k$ for $c_1,c_2$ with representing data; and a morphism $\nu_2\colon D_k\to D_2$ over $k$ which, for every $k$-scheme $T$ and every $T$-point $a$ of $D_k$, pulls the $D_2$-Poincaré bundle back, up to isomorphism, to the rigidification along $\varepsilon_2$ of the transport of $(\mathrm{hreps.poincare.pullbackAlong}\,a).L$ through `curveChange i₂`. The conclusion asserts the existence of a datum $G$ of type [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9), that is abelian groups $J^0_s\supseteq T$, $J_I$, $J_E$ with a surjection $\mathrm{proj}\colon J^0_s\to J_I\times J_E$ of kernel $T$, together with bijections of $J^0_s$, $J_I$, $J_E$ with the sets of $k$-sections of $D_k.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_1.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ respectively, such that in each of the three cases addition of group elements corresponds to the tensor product of the pullbacks of the respective Poincaré bundles along the corresponding sections (an isomorphism existing for each pair), such that for every $x\in J^0_s$ the first component of $\mathrm{proj}\,x$ corresponds to the section $x$ followed by the classifying morphism `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom` attached to $i_1$ and the second component to the section $x$ followed by $\nu_2$, and such that $T$ is isomorphic as an additive group to $\mathrm{Additive}(\mathrm{Fin}(n-1)\to k^\times)$.
--
--   This packages the classical description of the special fibre at $p$ of the identity component of the Néron model of the Jacobian of $X(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_1(p))$: for a curve whose special fibre is the union of two smooth components meeting in $n$ reduced points, $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the special fibre is an extension of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(C_1)\times\mathrm{Pic}^0(C_2)$ by a split torus of rank $n-1$, here in the bookkeeping form of a `NeronSpecialFibreGeom` datum with the group laws expressed through the Poincaré bundles. It feeds the construction of the norm-free part of the model of $X_1(Mp)$ and, through that, the semistable specialisation data used in the level-lowering step.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_neronSpecialFibreGeom_of_representsRelSubPic_baseChange_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

